To see if the required tools are ready on your system, you can perform a quick check directly from the Ubuntu terminal. The correct tool names are adb and fastboot (with an "s" instead of a "t"). [1, 2, 3] 
## Step 1: Check if ADB and Fastboot are Installed
Open your Ubuntu terminal (Ctrl + Alt + T) and run these two commands separately:

adb version

fastboot --version


* 
* If installed: The terminal will display version numbers (e.g., Android Debug Bridge version 1.0.41).
* If not installed: Ubuntu will output Command 'adb' not found or suggest an installation command. [3] 
* 

## Step 2: How to Install Them (If Missing)
If they are missing, run the following command to install the standard Android SDK platform tools via the official Ubuntu repositories: [2, 3] 

sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y android-sdk-platform-tools

