## Crucial Precautions for Rooting your Tecno KG6K (Spark 8)
Your device runs a MediaTek (MTK) chipset and is specifically on the KG6k-H6218MNOP-R-GL-230912V614 build. When preparing to root Android 11 with [Magisk](https://github.com/topjohnwu/Magisk) on this exact firmware, you must strictly follow these rules to avoid hard-bricking your phone: [4, 5] 

   1. Match the Boot Image Exactly: You must download the exact official firmware stock ROM matching your build string KG6k-H6218MNOP-R-GL-230912V614. Extracting and patching a boot.img or vbmeta.img from any other version (even a slightly different build date) will cause a bootloop. [5] 
   2. Unlock Bootloader via Fastboot: On Ubuntu, you will need to put your Tecno into Fastboot mode, check its status using fastboot devices, and then unlock it using:
   
   fastboot flashing unlock
   
   (Note: This factory-resets your phone, back up all your data first!) [4, 6] 
   3. Handle Disable Verification: Because it is an Android 11 MTK device, you will likely need to flash the patched boot image along with an empty or verified-boot disabling argument (fastboot flash vbmeta --disable-verity --disable-verification vbmeta.img) to bypass MediaTek's secure boot checks.

